     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena opened a savings account at the bank and learnt to pay using a phone.\n\"Money is safe in a bank,\" said her father."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "savings account",
     "UPI",
     "PIN"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A savings account keeps money safe and pays interest. A current account is used by businesses. A fixed deposit gives higher interest if money is kept for a fixed time.\nWe can withdraw money from an ATM, use debit cards and pay by UPI on a phone. Digital payments are fast but need care: never share the PIN or OTP.\nThe Reserve Bank of India regulates banks."
    }
